    "### Experiment 2: Zero-Shot Super Resolution\n",
    "\n",
    "This is a replication/extension of the experiment performed in the paper. Here, we train with the data at a fixed resolution (Nx = 128) but with PDE data at 1x, 2x, 4x, etc. the resolution. The idea of super resolution is that the network can still perform well at 4x the data resolution simply by having a PDE loss contribution at 4x. Since generating and evaluating PDE loss can be done for any point, we can create PDE loss data at any resolution and tune our model with it.\n",
    "\n",
    "Here we replicate the experiment from the original paper: train with data at fixed resolution and PDE loss at (2^n)x resolution. Then show that our model does not lose performance when testing up to (2^n)x resolution.\n",
    "\n",
    "Also, we normalize the total physics loss by the number of points sampled. This was one problem of experiment 1, and here we avoid extrapolating past the PDE training resolution."
   ]
